Executive summary
- Horizon Media finished the quarter with $5.2M in cash and generated $2.4M in revenue last quarter (average $800K/month). Our current reported net cash burn is $45K/month, which gives us roughly 115 months of runway at the current burn rate — a very healthy position that provides ample time to execute growth initiatives or optimize returns.

What this means
- With revenue at ~$800K/month and net cash outflow of only $45K/month, we are effectively close to break-even on a monthly basis. This gives us significant optionality: we can invest selectively in growth (marketing, product, or strategic hires), accelerate debt paydown, or delay any immediate fundraising needs.
- Key driver: strong revenue relative to operating spend. We should continue to monitor clients, AR timing, and any planned one-time investments that could materially alter monthly net cash flow.

Recommended next steps
