- Implied monthly cash outflows are ~ $1.125M (revenue + net burn), meaning we are spending substantially more than we are taking in this period. At that pace, we have roughly 16 months to execute on stabilization or raise additional capital.
- Primary risk drivers to call out: large one-time investments, hiring or contractor ramp, marketing spend, and timing of receivables or vendor payments.

Recommended next steps
- Rapidly segment the burn: fixed vs variable vs one-time. Identify the top 3 cost drivers contributing to the $325K net outflow and build options to reduce or defer them.
- Build three scenarios (Base, Conservative, Upside) for the next 12–18 months showing cash, burn, and runway under each.
