Horizon Media enters the planning period with $5.2M in cash and an implied net cash burn of approximately $325K/month, giving us roughly 16 months of runway. Last quarter revenue was $2.4M (≈$800K/month), and current burn dynamics indicate we have time to execute our growth and margin initiatives while we continue to optimize operating costs and revenue mix.

Detailed narrative (for internal materials):
As of today, Horizon Media has $5.2M in cash and an implied monthly net cash burn of approximately $325K, which results in an estimated runway of 16 months. Revenue for the most recent quarter was $2.4M (≈$800K/month). Under current assumptions, our cash position allows us to fund planned investments and normal operations for the next 16 months without additional financing, provided our revenue and expense trends remain consistent with current projections.

Key takeaways:
- Cash runway: ~16 months (5.2M / 325K).
- Revenue: last quarter $2.4M (≈$800K/month).
- Net burn: ≈$325K/month (implied).
- Annualized cash consumption: ≈$3.9M.
- Immediate priorities: strengthen topline growth to reduce net burn, target cost efficiencies to extend runway, and prepare a 12–18 month scenario plan (base/optimistic/downside).

Risks and mitigations:
- Downside risk: if revenue declines or planned margin improvements slip, runway will shorten — model a downside case where revenue drops X% and identify fixed vs variable costs to reprioritize quickly.
- Upside opportunity: if we accelerate new business or cross-sell, extra cash flow can be directed to strategic initiatives or reduce need for financing.

Recommended next steps:
- Deliver 3-scenario cash flow model (base / -20% revenue / +20% revenue) with monthly P&L and closing cash.
- Identify near-term cost levers that can reduce monthly cash consumption by 10–20% if needed.
- Re-run runway monthly and report to leadership with early warning triggers (e.g., runway ≤12 months, revenue shortfall >10%).

B — Narrative assuming burn = $45K/month (net burn) — runway ≈ 115 months
Executive summary (short):
