  - Cash balance (today)
  - Runway (months) and formula used
  - Gross burn and net burn (monthly)
  - Revenue run-rate (MRR or monthly average)
  - Cash conversion cycle / Days Sales Outstanding (DSO)
  - Committed vs pipeline revenue for next 12 months
- Risks & mitigants:
  - Risk: AR concentration / DSO increase → Mitigant: tighten terms, accelerate collections
  - Risk: One-off large payments → Mitigant: re-negotiate timing, stagger payments
  - Risk: Slower-than-forecast revenue → Mitigant: hiring freeze trigger, prioritize variable spend

Modeling & assumptions to include in materials
- Define burn clearly: gross cash outflows (payroll, rent, marketing, R&D, capex) and net burn (gross outflows – cash inflows).
- Show monthly granularity for 12 months, with line items: beginning cash, cash receipts (by source), cash payments (by category), net burn, ending cash.
