- Runway = Cash / Net burn (where “net burn” = cash outflows − cash inflows per month).
- If net burn = $45K/month, runway = 5.2M / 45K ≈ 115.6 months (≈ 9.6 years), not 16 months.
- If runway = 16 months, implied net burn = 5.2M / 16 = $325K/month.
- Revenue last quarter = $2.4M → ≈ $800K/month.
  - If net burn truly were $325K/month while revenue is $800K/month, that implies cash outflows ≈ $1,125K/month (because 1,125K − 800K = 325K).
  - If net burn = $45K/month with $800K revenue, that implies cash outflows ≈ $755K/month (because outflows − 800K = 45K).

Before finalizing any narrative we should confirm which figure is the authoritative “net burn” (the $45K or the 16-month runway). I’ll prepare narratives for both interpretations below so you can pick/edit.

